---
/**
 * The error summary, at the top of the form.
 *
 * Empty until a submission fails, and then it is the first thing focus moves
 * to — not the first invalid field. That ordering is the whole point of the
 * pattern: someone using a screen reader hears how many questions need
 * attention and what they are before being dropped into one of them, and
 * someone using a keyboard gets a jump list instead of a hunt down the page.
 *
 * role="alert" so the browser announces it the moment the script fills it in,
 * and tabindex="-1" so focus can be placed on it programmatically without
 * putting it into the tab order for everyone else.
 *
 * Red is state-blocked-deep, the one red in the palette that clears 4.5:1 on
 * white. The border is the fill value, which only has to clear 3:1 as a
 * non-text element.
 */
---

<div
	id="questionnaire-errors"
	role="alert"
	tabindex="-1"
	hidden
	class="mb-10 scroll-mt-8 border-l-2 border-state-blocked bg-state-blocked/[0.04] py-5 pr-5 pl-6"
>
	<p class="eyebrow text-state-blocked-deep" data-error-heading></p>

	<ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-1.5" data-error-list></ul>
</div>
